{
 "_why": "Hand-picked adhkar from an-Nawawi's al-Adhkar. The owner asked for this on 2026-09-17 («انتقي أنا بالإيد») after an automatic dua extractor was built and rejected: al-Adhkar's quotation marks are not a boundary, because «٣٧ - وروينا في ' صحيح البخاري ' عن حذيفةَ …» puts the BOOK's name in quotes and the supplication outside them, so a machine would have shipped a book title as a dua.",
 "_how": "NO ARABIC IS TYPED HERE. Each entry is a POINTER: a section index and an item index into the extractor's output, plus two short phrases that locate where the supplication starts and ends. The text that reaches the database is sliced out of that output at build time, exactly as the quotes corpus does it, so no diacritic can be lost in transcription. The phrases are a reading aid and never ship; one that stops matching fails the build loudly instead of half-matching and shipping a clipped supplication. `sha` is frozen on the first successful build and checked on every one after.",
 "_source": "scripts/build_azkar_from_adhkar.py output, from Shamela 1956 — an-Nawawi (d. 676 AH), عبد القادر الأرنؤوط's printing, whose apparatus is filtered out and never reaches the app.",
